window.LINES={"hello": "Hello, scientist! Welcome to Dr Celly's Clinic. That's me!", "knock": "Ooh, a patient! Come in!", "bolt_in": "It's Bolt, my robot friend. He says he feels funny.", "bolt_alive": "Bolt thinks feeling funny means he must be alive. Hmm!", "help": "Can you be my helper doctor today? Thank you!", "miccheck": "First, let's check I can hear you. Say: Hello, Bolt!", "heardyou": "I heard you! Bolt heard you too. Listen to him beep!", "nohear": "I can't hear you right now. That's okay. You can tap instead.", "tapmode": "Today you can tap your answers.", "cupboard": "Let's look in my very old medicine cupboard, from Ancient Egypt.", "dung": "Animal dung! Yuck! Egyptian doctors really used dung in medicines.", "nottry": "Please never try that at home!", "tools_intro": "Today, doctors use better tools. Which ones should we pick?", "t_steth": "A stethoscope. Doctors listen to how well your heart is beating.", "t_thermo": "A thermometer. Doctors measure your temperature.", "t_tests": "And doctors can test your blood and your urine.", "clue_intro": "Doctors look for clues. These clues are called symptoms.", "symptoms_mean": "Symptoms are changes in the way your body works.", "clue_play": "Three patients are waiting. Read their symptoms, and pick the illness.", "pt1": "Patient one has a sore throat and a runny nose.", "pt1_ans": "A cold! Sore throat and runny nose are symptoms of a cold.", "pt2": "Patient two has lots of spots on their skin.", "pt2_ans": "Spots are a clue too. That is a symptom!", "pt3": "Patient three feels hot, shivery and achy all over.", "pt3_ans": "That sounds like flu!", "evidence": "When symptoms match an illness, they are evidence.", "evidence_mean": "Evidence is information that helps us say if something is right or wrong.", "clue_done": "Brilliant detective work, doctor!", "watch": "Remember this bit from the video? Let's watch.", "organism": "A living thing is called an organism.", "question": "So, is Bolt an organism? Scientists have a test for it.", "buildintro": "First, we need the right words. Let's build them.", "tapbeats": "Tap the beats in the right order.", "w_organism": "This word means a living thing. It has four beats.", "w_sensitivity": "This one means sensing what is around you, and reacting. It has five beats.", "w_respiration": "This one releases energy from food, inside your cells. It has four beats.", "w_excretion": "This one means getting rid of waste. It has three beats.", "notyet": "Not that one yet. Which beat comes next?", "built": "You built it!", "drum": "Now tap the drum once for each beat, and say the beats with me.", "sayword": "Now say the whole word.", "again": "Let's try once more, slowly. Listen.", "yousay": "Now you say it.", "goodtry": "Good try! We'll practise that one again another day.", "n_organism": "Organism.", "n_sensitivity": "Sensitivity.", "n_respiration": "Respiration.", "n_excretion": "Excretion.", "s_or": "Or.", "s_gan": "Gan.", "s_is": "Is.", "s_m": "M.", "s_sen": "Sen.", "s_si": "Si.", "s_tiv": "Tiv.", "s_i": "I.", "s_ty": "Ty.", "s_res": "Res.", "s_pi": "Pi.", "s_ra": "Ra.", "s_tion": "Tion.", "s_ex": "Ex.", "s_cre": "Cre.", "ex_means": "Ex means out. Excretion gets waste out.", "sense_means": "Sense means feel. Sensitivity means feeling what is around you.", "wordsdone": "Four words built! Now we're ready for the checklist.", "meetgren": "Meet Mrs Gren! Her name is a mnemonic.", "mnemonic": "A mnemonic is a pattern of letters that helps you remember something.", "gren_job": "Mrs Gren helps us remember the seven life processes. Things all living things do.", "ordertiles": "Put her letters in order. M, R, S, G, R, E, N.", "tilewrong": "Hmm, not that letter yet. Say her name slowly.", "g_m": "M is for movement.", "g_r1": "R is for reproduction.", "g_s": "S is for sensitivity.", "g_g": "G is for growth.", "g_r2": "R is for respiration.", "g_e": "E is for excretion.", "g_n": "N is for nutrition.", "match_intro": "Now match each life process to what it means.", "d_move": "Movement means changing position.", "d_repro": "Reproduction means making copies of yourself. New living things.", "d_sense": "Sensitivity means detecting changes in the things around you.", "d_grow": "Growth means increasing in size.", "d_resp": "Respiration means releasing energy. You need food and oxygen.", "d_excr": "Excretion means getting rid of waste.", "d_nutr": "Nutrition means getting the substances you need to live.", "match_wrong": "Not quite. Read it out loud, and try another.", "grendone": "Mrs Gren is complete!", "allseven": "Remember: an organism does all seven. Not just some. All seven.", "breaktime": "You've worked hard, doctor. Time for a brain break!", "bb_intro": "Let's play Mrs Gren says. Only do it if Mrs Gren says!", "bb_move": "Mrs Gren says: wiggle your fingers. That's movement!", "bb_grow": "Mrs Gren says: crouch down small, then grow up tall, slowly.", "bb_breathe": "Mrs Gren says: breathe in slowly. And breathe out.", "bb_bite": "Mrs Gren says: take a big pretend bite of an apple. Crunch! That's nutrition.", "bb_sense": "Mrs Gren says: close your eyes. Can you hear a sound? That's sensitivity!", "bb_trick": "Now… touch your nose!", "bb_caught": "Ha! Mrs Gren didn't say! Did I catch you?", "bb_done": "Great moving! Your brain is ready again.", "bb_back": "Now let's test our patients.", "test_intro": "Let's go down Mrs Gren's checklist for Bolt. Tick or cross?", "b_move": "Can Bolt move?", "b_move_y": "Yes! Bolt rolls all over my clinic. Tick!", "b_sense": "Can Bolt sense things around him?", "b_sense_y": "Yes, he has a camera and sensors. Tick!", "b_grow": "Can Bolt grow bigger by himself?", "b_grow_n": "No. Bolt is wearing a tall hat, but that's cheating! Cross.", "b_repro": "Can Bolt make baby robots by himself?", "b_repro_n": "No! People build robots in a factory. Cross.", "b_verdict": "Bolt cannot do all seven. So Bolt is not an organism.", "zoom_in": "Oh! Who's honking? It's Zoom, Bolt's cousin. Zoom is a car!", "zoom_alive": "Zoom says he is definitely alive. Let's check him too.", "z_move": "Zoom can move. Tick.", "z_sense": "His alarm goes off if someone breaks in. That's a bit like sensing. Tick.", "z_resp": "He uses oxygen to release energy from his fuel. A bit like respiration. Tick.", "z_excr": "He puffs out exhaust gases. A bit like excretion. Tick.", "z_nutr": "And he needs fuel, like food. A bit like nutrition. Tick!", "z_five": "Five ticks! Is Zoom alive? Wait…", "z_grow": "Does Zoom grow bigger?", "z_babycar": "And have you ever seen a baby car?", "z_verdict": "No growth. No reproduction. So Zoom is not an organism.", "fire_in": "One more patient. A campfire! Fire moves, grows and uses oxygen.", "fire_check": "But can fire sense things around it? Can it reproduce?", "fire_verdict": "No. Fire cannot sense, and it cannot reproduce. So fire is not alive.", "repro_rule": "Here's a secret. Reproduction is the one thing no non-living thing can do.", "bolt_sad": "Oh, Bolt is beeping sadly.", "bolt_ok": "Don't worry, Bolt. You're not an organism, but you're the best friend ever!", "wait_intro": "Oh my! The waiting room is full of very strange patients.", "wait_how": "Is each one an organism? Say it, then tap the right box.", "c_cow": "A cow is an organism.", "c_car": "A car is not an organism. Remember Zoom!", "c_daffodil": "A daffodil is a plant. Plants are organisms.", "c_chair": "A chair is not alive. It's just a chair!", "c_goldfish": "A goldfish is an organism. It does all seven.", "c_coal": "Coal is not alive. It's a rock that burns.", "c_mouse": "A mouse is an organism.", "c_robot": "A robot is not an organism. Sorry, Bolt!", "c_octopus": "An octopus is an organism. Eight arms, all seven processes!", "c_rock": "A rock is not alive. It never even says hello.", "c_snake": "A snake is an organism.", "c_sun": "The Sun is very hot and bright, but it is not alive.", "c_cactus": "A cactus is a plant. It's an organism, even with spikes!", "c_gerbil": "A gerbil is an organism.", "c_cloud": "A cloud moves and grows, but it is not alive.", "c_river": "A river moves, but it is not alive.", "sort_wrong": "Hmm, check Mrs Gren. Can it do all seven?", "sort_done": "Waiting room sorted! What a clever doctor.", "lab_next": "Now, let's go to my clinic lab.", "lab_a": "Case one. Do plants respire? Let's test some seedlings.", "lab_a_set": "We put seedlings in a jar, above some limewater. Limewater goes milky with carbon dioxide.", "lab_a_wait": "Let's fast forward a few days. Whoosh!", "lab_a_q": "Look at the limewater. What happened?", "lab_a_ans": "It went milky! The seedlings made carbon dioxide.", "lab_a_end": "So plants respire, and they excrete carbon dioxide. That's our evidence!", "lab_b": "Case two. How old is this tree? Count the rings!", "lab_b_ring": "A tree grows one new ring every year.", "lab_b_wide": "A wide ring means a good growing year. A thin ring means a hard year.", "lab_b_keep": "Trees keep growing all their lives. Humans stop growing after a while.", "lab_b_joke": "Good news. You won't grow as tall as a tree!", "lab_c": "Case three. Sensitivity! Let's test it.", "lab_c_eye": "Shine a light at this eye. Watch the pupil, the black circle.", "lab_c_eye_a": "It got smaller! Your eyes sense bright light, and react.", "lab_c_hot": "Ouch, a hot pan! What does your hand do?", "lab_c_hot_a": "It moves away, fast! You sensed the heat and reacted.", "lab_d": "Quick question. How does a fish get oxygen?", "lab_d_ans": "A fish gets oxygen from water, using gills. We get oxygen from air, using lungs.", "lab_e": "And how do plants reproduce?", "lab_e_ans": "Many plants make flowers. Flowers make seeds and fruit. Some use insects to help.", "lab_f": "Do plants move?", "lab_f_ans": "Plants move parts of themselves, slowly. Animals usually move their whole body.", "lab_wrong": "Hmm, think again. You can do it.", "lab_done": "All cases solved!", "teach_intro": "Oh dear. All this doctoring has made me muddled. Can you teach me?", "m1": "Plants stay in one place, so plants don't move. Is that right?", "m1_fix": "Oh! Plants move parts of themselves, slowly. Thank you!", "m2": "Respiration is just another word for breathing. Is that right?", "m2_fix": "I see! Breathing brings oxygen in. Respiration releases energy, inside cells.", "m3": "Fire grows and moves, so fire must be alive. Is that right?", "m3_fix": "Of course! Fire cannot sense or reproduce. Not alive.", "m4": "Only animals respire. Plants don't. Is that right?", "m4_fix": "Silly me! The seedlings made the limewater milky. Plants respire too.", "m5": "Trees stop growing when they're grown up, just like people. Is that right?", "m5_fix": "Oh, they don't stop! Trees keep growing. People stop.", "teach_wrong": "Hmm, are you sure? Let's check our clues together.", "teach_done": "You're a brilliant teacher! I'm not muddled any more.", "finish": "Clinic closed! You helped every patient today.", "bigideas": "Remember: an organism is a living thing. It does all seven life processes. Mrs Gren helps you remember them.", "bolt_bye": "Bolt says thank you. He's happy being the best robot friend ever.", "cert": "Here is your certificate. You are a Life Process Detective!", "next": "Next time, we find out what organs do. See you soon, scientist!", "p1": "Well done!", "p2": "Brilliant!", "p3": "You got it!", "p4": "Super thinking!", "p5": "Great job!", "p6": "Fantastic!", "p7": "Yes! Even Bolt is dancing!"};
